    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $7\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is diagonal: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $7\\ne 0$, off the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
